foundation.question_text:
The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{x}{18}$ on $[0,6]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.8, xmax=7.2, ymin=-0.06, ymax=0.45, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6}, ytick={0.1,0.2,0.3}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:6] {x/18};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find $E(X)$.

foundation.solution_text:
$E(X)=\int_{0}^{6}x\cdot\frac{x}{18}\,dx$
$=\int_{0}^{6}\frac{x^{2}}{18}\,dx$
$=\left[\frac{x^{3}}{54}\right]_{0}^{6}$
$=\frac{216}{54}-0$
$=4$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.8, xmax=7.2, ymin=-0.06, ymax=0.45, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6}, ytick={0.1,0.2,0.3}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:6] {x/18};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:4,0) -- (axis cs:4,0.2222);
\node[above] at (axis cs:4,0.24) {$\mu=4$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{3x^{2}}{125}$ on $[0,5]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.7, xmax=6.2, ymin=-0.1, ymax=0.8, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5}, ytick={0.2,0.4,0.6}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:5] {3*x*x/125};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the expected value of $X$.

foundation.solution_text:
$E(X)=\int_{0}^{5}x\cdot\frac{3x^{2}}{125}\,dx$
$=\int_{0}^{5}\frac{3x^{3}}{125}\,dx$
$=\left[\frac{3x^{4}}{500}\right]_{0}^{5}$
$=\frac{3\times 625}{500}$
$=\frac{15}{4}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.7, xmax=6.2, ymin=-0.1, ymax=0.8, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5}, ytick={0.2,0.4,0.6}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:5] {3*x*x/125};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:3.75,0) -- (axis cs:3.75,0.3375);
\node[above left] at (axis cs:3.75,0.36) {$\mu=\frac{15}{4}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

