The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{2(3-x)}{9}$ on $[0,3]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.6, xmax=4.2, ymin=-0.1, ymax=0.85, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3}, ytick={0.2,0.4,0.6}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:3] {2*(3-x)/9};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find $E(X)$.

foundation.solution_text:
$E(X)=\int_{0}^{3}x\cdot\frac{2(3-x)}{9}\,dx$
$=\frac{2}{9}\int_{0}^{3}(3x-x^{2})\,dx$
$=\frac{2}{9}\left[\frac{3x^{2}}{2}-\frac{x^{3}}{3}\right]_{0}^{3}$
$=\frac{2}{9}\left(\frac{27}{2}-9\right)$
$=\frac{2}{9}\times\frac{9}{2}$
$=1$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.6, xmax=4.2, ymin=-0.1, ymax=0.85, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3}, ytick={0.2,0.4,0.6}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:3] {2*(3-x)/9};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:1,0) -- (axis cs:1,0.4444);
\node[above right] at (axis cs:1,0.47) {$\mu=1$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

